---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import portrait from '../assets/brijesh.jpg';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="About Brijesh Bhakta, a software engineer with 10 years of experience across backend, web, and mobile development."
  image={portrait.src}
>
  <header
    class="border-b border-rule pt-[clamp(4.5rem,9vw,9rem)] pb-[clamp(3rem,6vw,6rem)]"
  >
    <p
      class="mb-5 font-mono text-base font-semibold tracking-[0.12em] text-accent uppercase before:content-['//_']"
    >
      About
    </p>
    <h1
      class="mb-8 max-w-[980px] font-serif text-[clamp(3.4rem,7vw,7rem)] leading-[0.98] font-normal tracking-[-0.035em]"
    >
      Wide perspective. Careful execution.
    </h1>
  </header>
  <section
    class="grid grid-cols-[minmax(240px,0.8fr)_2fr] items-start gap-[clamp(2.5rem,7vw,8rem)] border-b border-rule py-[clamp(5rem,10vw,10rem)] max-mobile:grid-cols-1"
  >
    <img
      class="aspect-[1/1.08] w-full border-b-8 border-accent object-cover grayscale"
      src={portrait.src}
      width={portrait.width}
      height={portrait.height}
      alt="Brijesh Bhakta"
    />
    <div
      class="max-w-[770px] [&>p:first-of-type]:font-serif [&>p:first-of-type]:text-[clamp(1.8rem,3.5vw,3.2rem)] [&>p:first-of-type]:leading-[1.2]"
    >
      <p>
        I’m Brijesh, a software engineer who has spent the last decade working
        across the layers that make a product useful.
      </p>
      <p>
        My background includes backend services, data-heavy web applications,
        identity systems, payments, and mobile-connected products. That range
        helps me trace a problem from the interface through the API and into the
        underlying system without losing sight of the person using it.
      </p>
      <p>
        I graduated in Computer Engineering from Uka Tarsadia University in 2016
        and began my professional career working across .NET, Node.js, and
        full-stack product development. I’ve kept the same curiosity since:
        learn the system, make the trade-offs explicit, and leave the code
        easier to understand.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="border-b border-rule py-[clamp(5rem,10vw,10rem)]">
    <p
      class="mb-5 font-mono text-base font-semibold tracking-[0.12em] text-accent uppercase before:content-['//_']"
    >
      Working approach
    </p>
    <div
      class="grid grid-cols-3 gap-12 max-mobile:grid-cols-1 [&_h3]:font-serif [&_h3]:text-[1.7rem] [&_h3]:font-normal [&_p]:text-secondary"
    >
      <article>
        <h3>Understand the whole</h3><p>
          Good technical choices start with the user, the constraints, and the
          surrounding system—not a preferred tool.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h3>Make complexity legible</h3><p>
          Clear boundaries, direct communication, and maintainable code make
          products easier to operate and evolve.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h3>Keep learning practical</h3><p>
          New technology matters when it improves reliability, speed, or the
          experience—not because it is new.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
